[node name="DeathPlane" type="Node3D" parent="."]
script = ExtResource("261_death")
MarioPath = NodePath("../PlayerSpawner/Mario")
metadata/_sms_note = "Pass 261: the DEATH PLANE -- the game's death-plane floor under the void (TMario::thinkSituation, MarioMove.cpp 1886): the frame Mario's feet drop through this node's height (anywhere: the plane has no edges) he takes the fall death -- game over, HP 0, he falls on with no control, the cry, the camera's eye stops and watches him fall away, the iris 2 s on, TOO BAD!, a life down, this course again from its start with no intro. At y 0 = the game's own height: the vanilla map.col of the Hillside Cave Secret and the Secret of Ricco Tower hold nothing but this plane at y 0 (and a catch floor at -16000 units); the courses' pieces sit 1700-3400 units over it. This course's own collision was not to hand (its lowest piece is 56.4 m over the plane); the sheet is the course's bounds + 60 m. The red Preview sheet shows it here in the editor and is hidden in play. Active off = no death (he falls on for ever, as before)."

